  "stem": "In the \\(xy\\)-plane, the point \\((k, k)\\) lies on the graph of \\(y = \\frac{2}{3}x - 4\\). What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "mcq",
  "choices": {
    "A": "\\(12\\)",
    "B": "\\(-4\\)",
    "C": "\\(-6\\)",
    "D": "\\(-12\\)"
  },
  "answer": "D",
  "spr_answers": null,
  "solution": [
    "Substitute \\(x = k\\) and \\(y = k\\): \\(k = \\frac{2}{3}k - 4\\).",
    "Subtract \\(\\frac{2}{3}k\\): \\(\\frac{1}{3}k = -4\\), so \\(k = -12\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": {
    "A": "Incorrect. \\(\\frac{1}{3}k = -4\\) gives a negative \\(k\\); check: \\(\\frac{2}{3}(12) - 4 = 4 \\ne 12\\).",
    "B": "Incorrect. \\(-4\\) is the \\(y\\)-intercept; the point \\((0, -4)\\) does not have equal coordinates.",
    "C": "Incorrect. Check: \\(\\frac{2}{3}(-6) - 4 = -8 \\ne -6\\).",
    "D": "Correct. \\(k = \\frac{2}{3}k - 4\\) gives \\(\\frac{1}{3}k = -4\\), so \\(k = -12\\)."
  },
  "traps": {
    "A": "sign_error",
    "B": "concept",
    "C": "arithmetic"
  },
  "verify": "k = symbols('k')\nsol = solve(Eq(k, Rational(2, 3)*k - 4), k)\nassert sol == [-12]\nassert value(choices[answer]) == -12\nassert all(value(choices[k]) != -12 for k in choices if k != answer)",
